-override" data-step="t2-override"><span>🎭</span> 4. Method Overriding</a></nav><div class="lx-sections" style="margin-top:24px"><section id="t2-parent" class="lx-chal" data-part="0"><div class="lx-stage"><div class="lx-stage-ic"><span aria-hidden="true">🌳</span><span class="st"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M11.525 2.295a.53.53 0 0 1 .95 0l2.31 4.679a2.123 2.123 0 0 0 1.595 1.16l5.166.756a.53.53 0 0 1 .294.904l-3.736 3.638a2.123 2.123 0 0 0-.611 1.878l.882 5.14a.53.53 0 0 1-.771.56l-4.618-2.428a2.122 2.122 0 0 0-1.973 0L6.396 21.01a.53.53 0 0 1-.77-.56l.881-5.139a2.122 2.122 0 0 0-.611-1.879L2.16 9.795a.53.53 0 0 1 .294-.906l5.165-.755a2.122 2.122 0 0 0 1.597-1.16z"/></svg></span></div><div style="min-width:0"><small style="color:#9A6735">Part 1 of 4</small><h2>Parent and Child Classes</h2></div><div class="rule"></div></div><div class="lx-step" data-substep="learn"><div class="lx-g2"><div class="lx-card lx-learn"><div class="lx-learn-top"><div><span class="lx-tag">Learn</span></div><p class="lx-prose"><strong>Inheritance</strong> lets a child class acquire the attributes and methods of a parent class. It models an <em>is-a</em> relationship: a Dog <strong>is an</strong> Animal. Put the parent&#039;s name in parentheses to inherit.</p><div class="lx-facts"><div class="lx-fact"><small>Syntax</small><b>class Child(Parent):</b></div><div class="lx-fact"><small>Relationship</small><b>is-a</b></div><div class="lx-fact"><small>Benefit</small><b>code reuse</b></div></div><div class="lx-ana"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M16 3a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v6a2 2 0 0 0 2 2 1 1 0 0 1 1 1v1a2 2 0 0 1-2 2 1 1 0 0 0-1 1v2a1 1 0 0 0 1 1 6 6 0 