e Changing</h2></div><div class="rule"></div></div><div class="lx-step" data-substep="learn"><div class="lx-g2"><div class="lx-card lx-learn"><div class="lx-learn-top"><div><span class="lx-tag">Learn</span></div><p class="lx-prose">The point of hiding data is control. Instead of letting anyone overwrite a value, expose a <strong>method</strong> that checks the new value first. Bad input is rejected and the object stays valid.</p><div class="lx-facts"><div class="lx-fact"><small>Hide</small><b>__balance</b></div><div class="lx-fact"><small>Gate</small><b>deposit()</b></div><div class="lx-fact"><small>Result</small><b>always valid</b></div></div><div class="lx-ana"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M16 3a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v6a2 2 0 0 0 2 2 1 1 0 0 1 1 1v1a2 2 0 0 1-2 2 1 1 0 0 0-1 1v2a1 1 0 0 0 1 1 6 6 0 0 0 6-6V5a2 2 0 0 0-2-2z"/><path d="M5 3a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v6a2 2 0 0 0 2 2 1 1 0 0 1 1 1v1a2 2 0 0 1-2 2 1 1 0 0 0-1 1v2a1 1 0 0 0 1 1 6 6 0 0 0 6-6V5a2 2 0 0 0-2-2z"/></svg><p>A bank teller checks every deposit slip instead of letting you reach into the vault.</p></div></div><div class="lx-learn-ex"><small>Example</small><pre class="lx-code"><span class="k">def</span> deposit(<span class="sf">self</span>, amount):
